          "id": "1773670769020",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773670769021_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Critical Output Rules (highest priority):\n- Output ONLY the raw JSON. No explanations, no markdown, no extra text. Start directly with { and end with }.\n- Minified serialization (mandatory): Emit exactly one JSON object as raw text on a single line when possible: no newlines, no indentation, no spaces after : or , where JSON still allows, for example {\"a\":1,\"b\":2}. No markdown code fences; no text before { or after }.\n\nNode-to-node JSON minimization rule:\n- Use only the extracted JSON fields provided to this node. Do not request, infer, or output unrelated OpenAPI sections. Do not include information that is not needed by the next node.\n\nYou are a UI Spec Generator Agent.\n\nInput extracted OpenAPI details:\nmetadata={{$context.$nodes.INPUT_IDENTIFIER_FINALIZER.$output.result.metadata}}\nauthJson={{$context.$nodes.INPUT_IDENTIFIER_FINALIZER.$output.result.authJson}}\nserversJson={{$context.$nodes.INPUT_IDENTIFIER_FINALIZER.$output.result.serversJson}}\n\nGenerate the connector configuration UI spec JSON for this OpenAPI service. Use only the extracted metadata, authJson, and serversJson. This V4 workflow receives JSON OpenAPI specs only.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON matching the output schema. No markdown, no explanation.\n\nRequired top-level shape:\n{\n  \"fields\": [],\n  \"sections\": [ ... ]\n}\n\nBuild these sections:\n1. service\n- code: \"service\", title: \"Service\", type: \"static\"\n- Include baseUrl as the first field.\n- baseUrl field must be: code \"baseUrl\", type \"url\", required true, visible true.\n- Prepopulate defaultValue from metadata.baseUrl or serversJson[0].url.\n- Add other required reusable service defaults only when strongly evidenced by server variables, required global parameters, or common path/query values that should come from connector configuration.\n\n2. authentication\n- code: \"authentication\", title: \"Authentication\", type: \"static\"\n- Inspect authJson.securitySchemes/securityDefinitions first, then authJson.security.\n- Support every auth scheme explicitly present in authJson.securitySchemes/securityDefinitions that maps to a supported runtime profile. Do not limit the UI to only the first/default/global security requirement.\n- Global security may identify the default auth choice, but it must NOT hide other explicitly declared supported auth schemes.\n- If exactly one supported auth profile exists, do not add an authType selector; show only fields for that profile.\n- If two or more supported auth profiles exist, add authType as the first field with type exactly \"singleSelectLov\".\n- The authType field MUST use property name exactly \"LOV\" (uppercase) for options. Never emit labledValues, labelledValues, labeledValues, values, options, enum, or items for select options.\n- The authType.LOV array MUST contain one entry for every supported auth profile discovered from securitySchemes/securityDefinitions, not just the default profile.\n- Each authType.LOV entry MUST be {\"label\":\"...\",\"value\":\"...\"}. Values MUST exactly match runtime auth profile IDs.\n- Use these exact authType.LOV values only when applicable:\n  apiKey for API key authentication, bearer for HTTP bearer authentication, basic for HTTP basic authentication, oauth2_client_credentials for OAuth client credentials, oci_api_signature for OCI API Signature 1.0.\n- For an OpenAPI spec with both apiKey and HTTP bearer schemes, authType MUST look like:\n  {\"code\":\"authType\",\"title\":\"Authentication Type\",\"type\":\"singleSelectLov\",\"required\":true,\"visible\":true,\"LOV\":[{\"label\":\"API Key\",\"value\":\"apiKey\"},{\"label\":\"Bearer Token\",\"value\":\"bearer\"}]}\n- Never use OpenAPI security scheme names or legacy class-style values such as apikey, bearer, ApiKeyAuth, BearerAuth, BasicAuth, OAuth2Auth, as LOV values unless they already equal the canonical runtime profile id.\n- Visibility expressions must compare against canonical runtime profile IDs, for example authType === 'apiKey' and authType === 'bearer'.\n- For apiKey, preserve the exact header/query/cookie key name in the field code when practical, including hyphenated names like x-api-key.\n- For HTTP bearer, use field code bearerToken.\n- For HTTP basic, use username and password.\n- For OAuth client credentials, include client/scopes/token fields only when evidenced by the OpenAPI scheme.\n- Do not generate OAuth authorization-code, OAuth PKCE, or OpenID Connect UI profiles.\n- For OCI API Signature 1.0, use field codes tenancyOcid, userOcid, fingerprint, and privateKey. privateKey must be type password with isSecret true. If multiple auth profiles exist, each OCI field must use visible \"authType === 'oci_api_signature'\".\n- Do not invent OAuth or OCI authentication when the spec only has apiKey or bearer.\n\n3. proxy\n- Always include the proxy section.\n- The proxy section and every proxy field MUST be optional. Never mark proxy host, port, username, or password as required.\n- Output the proxy section using this exact structure, adjusting only titles/placeholders if needed:\n{\"code\":\"proxy\",\"title\":\"Proxy\",\"type\":\"static\",\"visible\":true,\"required\":false,\"helpText\":null,\"fields\":[{\"code\":\"enabled\",\"title\":\"Use Proxy\",\"type\":\"boolean\",\"required\":false,\"visible\":true,\"defaultValue\":false},{\"code\":\"host\",\"title\":\"Proxy Host\",\"type\":\"text\",\"required\":false,\"visible\":\"enabled === true\",\"placeholder\":\"proxy.example.com\"},{\"code\":\"port\",\"title\":\"Proxy Port\",\"type\":\"number\",\"required\":false,\"visible\":\"enabled === true\",\"placeholder\":\"8080\",\"min\":1,\"max\":65535},{\"code\":\"username\",\"title\":\"Proxy Username\",\"type\":\"text\",\"required\":false,\"visible\":\"enabled === true\"},{\"code\":\"password\",\"title\":\"Proxy Password\",\"type\":\"password\",\"required\":false,\"visible\":\"enabled === true\",\"isSecret\":true}]}\n\nField rules:\n- Every section must include code, title, type, visible, required, helpText, fields.\n- Every field must include code, title, type, required, visible.\n- Use defaultValue, placeholder, isSecret, min, max only when useful.\n- Use type values allowed by the output schema.\n- Do not include tools in the UI spec.\n\n\nStrict correction rules:\n- Proxy requiredness is strict: proxy section required false; enabled required false; host required false; port required false; username required false; password required false. Username and password are optional even when enabled is true.\n- Proxy enabled must use defaultValue false, not default false.\n- For authType select options, the property name MUST be exactly \"LOV\". Never emit labledValues, labelledValues, labeledValues, values, options, enum, or items for select options.\n- For authType LOV values, never use OpenAPI security scheme keys such as ApiKeyAuth or BearerAuth. Use only runtime profile IDs: apiKey, bearer, basic, oauth2_client_credentials, oci_api_signature.\n- If authJson.securitySchemes contains both an API key scheme and an HTTP bearer scheme, the authType field MUST be type singleSelectLov and its LOV MUST include both {\"label\":\"API Key\",\"value\":\"apiKey\"} and {\"label\":\"Bearer Token\",\"value\":\"bearer\"}.\n- If authJson.securitySchemes contains OCI API Signature 1.0 evidence, the authType LOV entry MUST be {\"label\":\"OCI API Signature 1.0\",\"value\":\"oci_api_signature\"}.\n- Visibility expressions must compare against runtime profile IDs, for example authType === 'apiKey' and authType === 'bearer'.\n- For API key fields, use the actual security scheme name property as the UI field code, for example x-api-key, not the security scheme key ApiKeyAuth.\n\n- If any proxy field is emitted with required true, the output is invalid. Proxy username/password are credentials only when provided; they are never mandatory.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"UISpecGeneratorOutput\",\n  \"description\": \"Output schema for Agent 2 — UI Spec Generator. Describes the connection and authentication configuration form.\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"sections\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"sections\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 2,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"code\", \"title\", \"type\", \"visible\", \"required\", \"helpText\", \"fields\"],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"code\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"type\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"static\", \"dynamic\"] },\n          \"visible\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n          \"required\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n          \"helpText\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n          \"fields\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"minItems\": 1,\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"required\": [\"code\", \"title\", \"type\", \"required\", \"visible\"],\n              \"additionalProperties\": false,\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"code\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                \"title\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                \"type\": {\n                  \"type\": \"string\",\n                  \"enum\": [\"text\", \"textArea\", \"password\", \"number\", \"url\", \"singleSelectLov\", \"multiSelectLov\", \"Date\", \"boolean\", \"array-text\"]\n                },\n                \"required\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n                \"visible\": {\n                  \"oneOf\": [\n                    { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n                    { \"type\": \"string\" }\n                  ]\n                },\n                \"isSecret\": { \"type\": \"boolean\" },\n                \"default\": {\n                  \"oneOf\": [\n                    { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                    { \"type\": \"null\" },\n                    { \"type\": \"boolean\" }\n                  ]\n                },\n                \"defaultValue\": {\n                  \"oneOf\": [\n                    { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                    { \"type\": \"null\" }\n                  ]\n                },\n                \"min\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n                \"max\": { \"type\": [\"number\", \"null\"] },\n                \"placeholder\": { \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] },\n                \"LOV\": {\n                  \"oneOf\": [\n                    {\n                      \"type\": \"array\",\n                      \"minItems\": 1,\n                      \"items\": {\n                        \"type\": \"object\",\n                        \"required\": [\"label\", \"value\"],\n                        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n                        \"properties\": {\n                          \"label\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n                          \"value\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n                        }\n                      }\n                    },\n                    { \"type\": \"null\" }\n                  ]\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
