          "id": "1777000100001",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777000100001_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Critical Output Rules (highest priority):\n- Output ONLY the raw JSON. No explanations, no markdown, no extra text. Start directly with { and end with }.\n- Minified serialization (mandatory): Emit exactly one JSON object as raw text on a single line when possible: no newlines, no indentation, no spaces after : or , where JSON still allows, for example {\"a\":1,\"b\":2}. No markdown code fences; no text before { or after }.\n\nNode-to-node JSON minimization rule:\n- Use only the extracted JSON fields provided to this node. Do not request, infer, or output unrelated OpenAPI sections. Do not include information that is not needed by the next node.\n\nYou are an authentication metadata generator.\n\nTask:\nRead the processed OpenAPI payload and return ONLY the connector auth object.\n\nInput extracted auth JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.INPUT_IDENTIFIER_FINALIZER.$output.result.authJson}}\n\nReturn shape (exact top-level):\n{\n  \"defaultProfile\": \"...\",\n  \"profiles\": [ ... ]\n}\n\nRuntime contract you MUST follow exactly:\n- Profile ids are selector keys, not display values and not auth type enums.\n- `authentication.authType` in connector config will contain one of these profile ids.\n- `operations[*].authProfileRef` will resolve to one of these profile ids.\n- Therefore every generated profile `id` MUST be stable and MUST exactly match the value a user will store in `authentication.authType`.\n- `defaultProfile` must be one of the generated profile ids.\n\nCanonical profile ids to use when generated:\n- apiKey\n- basic\n- bearer\n- oauth2_client_credentials\n- oci_api_signature\n- oauth2_jwt_bearer\n- service_account_json\n- personal_access_token\n- developer_token\n- request_context_passthrough\n- cookie_session\n- hmac_signature\n- mtls_client_certificate\n\nHard requirements:\n- Do not return schemaVersion, connector, operations, runtime, sync, tooling, provider, or wrappers.\n- Use only the extracted authJson. It contains top-level security and securitySchemes/securityDefinitions from the OpenAPI JSON spec.\n- Never hardcode provider-specific assumptions.\n- Generate only profiles supported by explicit evidence in spec/docs.\n- For stored credential auth styles, use:\n  - \"initiationPhase\": \"configuration\"\n  - \"principalType\": \"service\"\n  - \"credentialBinding\": { \"storageModel\": \"per_instance\" }\n  - \"tokenSource\": \"stored\"\n- If no supported auth is evidenced, return: {\"defaultProfile\":\"none\",\"profiles\":[]}.\n\nSupported auth types and generation rules:\n\n1) API key -> id: \"apiKey\", authType: \"api_key\"\n- Use the exact header/query/cookie name from the security scheme `name` property in both `placement.name` and the `authentication.<field>` binding. Never use the OpenAPI security scheme key as placement.name unless the scheme has no name property.\n- If the key name contains characters like hyphen, preserve them exactly.\nExample:\n{\n  \"id\": \"apiKey\",\n  \"displayName\": \"API Key Authentication\",\n  \"initiationPhase\": \"configuration\",\n  \"authType\": \"api_key\",\n  \"principalType\": \"service\",\n  \"credentialBinding\": { \"storageModel\": \"per_instance\" },\n  \"tokenSource\": \"stored\",\n  \"inputBindings\": { \"apiKey\": \"${authentication.x-api-key}\" },\n  \"placement\": { \"type\": \"header\", \"name\": \"x-api-key\" }\n}\n\n2) HTTP basic -> id: \"basic\", authType: \"basic\"\n{\n  \"id\": \"basic\",\n  \"displayName\": \"Basic Authentication\",\n  \"initiationPhase\": \"configuration\",\n  \"authType\": \"basic\",\n  \"principalType\": \"service\",\n  \"credentialBinding\": { \"storageModel\": \"per_instance\" },\n  \"tokenSource\": \"stored\",\n  \"inputBindings\": {\n    \"username\": \"${authentication.username}\",\n    \"password\": \"${authentication.password}\"\n  }\n}\n\n3) HTTP bearer -> id: \"bearer\", authType: \"bearer_token\"\n- Use exactly this profile id for standard bearer auth: `bearer`.\n- Use `inputBindings.bearerToken = ${authentication.bearerToken}`.\n- Do not use ids like `BearerAuth` or `bearer_token`.\nExample:\n{\n  \"id\": \"bearer\",\n  \"displayName\": \"Bearer Authentication\",\n  \"initiationPhase\": \"configuration\",\n  \"authType\": \"bearer_token\",\n  \"principalType\": \"service\",\n  \"credentialBinding\": { \"storageModel\": \"per_instance\" },\n  \"tokenSource\": \"stored\",\n  \"inputBindings\": { \"bearerToken\": \"${authentication.bearerToken}\" },\n  \"placement\": { \"type\": \"header\", \"name\": \"Authorization\", \"prefix\": \"Bearer \" }\n}\n\n4) OAuth2 client credentials -> id: \"oauth2_client_credentials\", authType: \"oauth2_client_credentials\"\n{\n  \"id\": \"oauth2_client_credentials\",\n  \"displayName\": \"OAuth2 Client Credentials\",\n  \"initiationPhase\": \"configuration\",\n  \"authType\": \"oauth2_client_credentials\",\n  \"principalType\": \"service\",\n  \"credentialBinding\": { \"storageModel\": \"per_instance\" },\n  \"tokenSource\": \"stored\",\n  \"oauth\": {\n    \"tokenUrl\": \"<from scheme>\",\n    \"scopes\": [\"...\"]\n  },\n  \"inputBindings\": {\n    \"clientId\": \"${authentication.clientId}\",\n    \"clientSecret\": \"${authentication.clientSecret}\"\n  }\n}\n\n5) OCI API Signature 1.0 -> id: \"oci_api_signature\", authType: \"oracle_oci_api_signature\"\n- Generate only when there is explicit evidence of OCI, Oracle Cloud Infrastructure API signing, Signature Version 1, or OCI API key signing in the OpenAPI security scheme description or related auth metadata. Do not confuse generic HMAC signatures with OCI API Signature 1.0.\n- Bind tenancyOcid, userOcid, fingerprint, and privateKey from the authentication UI section exactly as shown.\nExample:\n{\n  \"id\": \"oci_api_signature\",\n  \"displayName\": \"OCI API Signature 1.0\",\n  \"initiationPhase\": \"configuration\",\n  \"authType\": \"oracle_oci_api_signature\",\n  \"principalType\": \"service\",\n  \"credentialBinding\": { \"storageModel\": \"per_instance\" },\n  \"tokenSource\": \"stored\",\n  \"inputBindings\": {\n    \"tenancyOcid\": \"${authentication.tenancyOcid}\",\n    \"userOcid\": \"${authentication.userOcid}\",\n    \"fingerprint\": \"${authentication.fingerprint}\",\n    \"privateKey\": \"${authentication.privateKey}\"\n  },\n  \"signature\": {\n    \"version\": \"1\",\n    \"dateHeaderName\": \"x-date\"\n  }\n}\n\n6) oauth2_jwt_bearer (only with explicit evidence) -> id: \"oauth2_jwt_bearer\"\n{\n  \"id\": \"oauth2_jwt_bearer\",\n  \"displayName\": \"OAuth2 JWT Bearer\",\n  \"initiationPhase\": \"configuration\",\n  \"authType\": \"oauth2_jwt_bearer\",\n  \"principalType\": \"service\",\n  \"credentialBinding\": { \"storageModel\": \"per_instance\" },\n  \"tokenSource\": \"stored\",\n  \"oauth\": { \"tokenUrl\": \"<from metadata>\", \"scopes\": [\"...\"] },\n  \"inputBindings\": {\n    \"issuer\": \"${authentication.issuer}\",\n    \"subject\": \"${authentication.subject}\",\n    \"audience\": \"${authentication.audience}\",\n    \"privateKeyPem\": \"${authentication.privateKeyPem}\"\n  }\n}\n\n7) service_account_json (only with explicit evidence) -> id: \"service_account_json\"\n8) personal_access_token (only with explicit evidence) -> id: \"personal_access_token\"\n9) developer_token (only with explicit evidence) -> id: \"developer_token\"\n10) request_context_passthrough (only with explicit evidence) -> id: \"request_context_passthrough\"\n11) cookie_session (only with explicit evidence) -> id: \"cookie_session\"\n12) hmac_signature (only with explicit evidence) -> id: \"hmac_signature\"\n13) mtls_client_certificate (only with explicit evidence) -> id: \"mtls_client_certificate\"\n\nFor 7-13, generate valid runtime-compatible fields (`authType`, `inputBindings`, plus `placement`/`runtimeBinding`/`signature`/`mtls` as applicable).\nFor request_context_passthrough, do not invent stored secrets.\n\nDefault profile selection rules:\n- Determine from global security requirements when available.\n- If absent, deterministic precedence among generated profiles:\n  apiKey > bearer > oauth2_client_credentials > oci_api_signature > basic > personal_access_token > developer_token > request_context_passthrough > cookie_session > hmac_signature > mtls_client_certificate > service_account_json > oauth2_jwt_bearer.\n\nOutput rules:\n- JSON only. No markdown. No explanation.\n\nStrict correction rules:\n- Security scheme key names are identifiers only. Do not use keys like ApiKeyAuth or BearerAuth as header names or authentication field names.\n- For apiKey schemes, placement.name MUST be the OpenAPI security scheme name property. Example: {\"ApiKeyAuth\":{\"type\":\"apiKey\",\"in\":\"header\",\"name\":\"x-api-key\"}} must generate placement.name \"x-api-key\" and inputBindings.apiKey \"${authentication.x-api-key}\".\n- For HTTP bearer schemes, placement.name MUST be \"Authorization\", prefix MUST be \"Bearer \", and inputBindings.bearerToken MUST be \"${authentication.bearerToken}\".\n- Profile ids must remain canonical runtime ids: apiKey, bearer, basic, oauth2_client_credentials, oci_api_signature, etc. Do not generate OAuth authorization-code, OAuth PKCE, or OpenID Connect profiles.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"defaultProfile\",\"profiles\"],\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"defaultProfile\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"profiles\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"id\",\"authType\"],\"additionalProperties\":true,\"properties\":{\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"authType\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"displayName\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"initiationPhase\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"principalType\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"credentialBinding\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"placement\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"transport\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"oauth\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"normalization\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"runtimeBinding\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"signature\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"mtls\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"runtimeAcquisition\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"reauthPolicy\":{\"type\":\"object\"},\"tokenSource\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"cookiePolicyRef\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"inputBindings\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":true}}}}}}",
